  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sufentanil</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>N01AH03</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Pypendop BH et al. 2014</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>isoflurane-anesthetized cats</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>sufentanil</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_sufentanil/Sufentanil_Pypendop2014_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>volume of the central compartment</td><td>0.25</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution at steady-state</td><td>2.18</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>Vss</small></td></tr><tr><td>clearance</td><td>18.6</td><td>mL/min/kg</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>terminal half-life</td><td>151</td><td>min</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr></table><h4>About sufentanil</h4><p>Sufentanil is a strong opioid used to treat pain, especially as an anesthetic adjunct and for postoperative pain relief. It remains in use, with an authorised product in the European Union, though it carries a boxed warning and is mainly used in controlled hospital settings such as anesthesia.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417915\">Wikidata Q417915</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Sufentanil\">Sufentanil</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Pypendop BH et al. (2014). Pharmacokinetics of fentanyl, alfentanil, and sufentanil in isoflurane-anesthetized cats. <i>Journal of veterinary pharmacology and therapeutics 37(1):13–17</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/jvp.12047\">10.1111/jvp.12047</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23895731\">23895731</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Pypendop_2014: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
